<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Manuel González Flores</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1833–1893</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Manuel González Flores was a Mexican general and president from 1880 to 1884, a close ally of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/porfirio-diaz">Porfirio Díaz</a>, who held the office between Díaz's first and second terms. His government extended railways and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/telegraph">telegraph</a> lines but faced charges of corruption and riots over a new nickel coinage. Díaz returned to the presidency in 1884.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/manuel-gonzalez-flores.jpg" alt="Manuel González Flores" width="320" height="421" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:President_Manuel_Gonzalez.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
